WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.250
He actually blocked a kick
with his hand, forearm.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.610
Don't do that at home, folks.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.693
Hand or forearm against shin,

00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:11.884
like, look at this, who wins?

00:00:11.884 --> 00:00:13.498
Hi, my name's Miriam Nakamoto.

00:00:13.498 --> 00:00:15.470
I'm an eight-time Muay
Thai world champion,

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.880
and I've been doing it
for over two decades.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.610
Today we're going to be
looking at Muay Thai scenes

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.168
from movies and TV,

00:00:21.168 --> 00:00:23.259
and we're going to
judge how real they are.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.790
Her form is great on those elbows.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.615
So, elbows is the shortest-range weapon

00:00:34.615 --> 00:00:36.060
of a Muay Thai fight.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.868
There's a up elbow,

00:00:38.843 --> 00:00:41.609
and then there's round elbows.

00:00:41.609 --> 00:00:43.320
And then there's a Tomahawk elbow,

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.610
and then there's spike elbows too.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.900
So what she's doing in this
scene is a spike elbow.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.941
In a Muay Thai fight,

00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:51.357
I would not elbow anywhere but the head.

00:00:51.357 --> 00:00:52.940
Because if you're elbowing somewhere else,

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.460
that means your head is down,

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:57.400
where there's a lot of danger.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.492
So that was very, very, very realistic.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:04.290
That, no. That's not Muay Thai.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:06.940
What Muay Thai is, is
you take a boxing match,

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:09.590
and then you add not only punches,

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.975
but you add in kicks.

00:01:10.975 --> 00:01:14.955
And not only kicks, you can also elbow,

00:01:14.955 --> 00:01:17.627
knee, and standing grappling.

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:23.400
That kick is awesome.
I need to learn that.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.820
The spinning kick looked
correct. It's not common.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.750
You wouldn't see that very
often in a Muay Thai fight.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.710
Usually you just see round
kick, you see the foot jabs,

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.080
you see the low kick,
a question-mark kick,

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.100
where it comes up here
and then it goes around.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.141
Well, I'll say 8 out of 10,

00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:42.030
just 'cause that whole jumping
up on the shoulders thing

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.450
and flinging yourself down is like,

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.290
no, that's not gonna happen.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.540
But everything else looked great.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.220
That tree, I think that's doable,

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.040
but in America, that is not common.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.140
People do kick tires, not full blast

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:57.970
but just kind of repetitive stress,

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:00.020
or they'll kick really heavy, hard bags.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:02.720
I would kick really hard Thai pads.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.595
Or you could kick a banana tree.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.120
It's absolutely 100% realistic

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.390
and vital to condition your shins.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:16.673
Shin is your shield.

00:02:16.673 --> 00:02:18.231
You block kicks with your shins,

00:02:18.231 --> 00:02:20.410
you apply damage with your shins.

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:22.570
But he keeps pointing his toes.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.900
There he is, pointing his toes some more.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.630
We don't do the toe-pointing thing.

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:30.004
Because as a Muay Thai kick,
you want to cut them in half.

00:02:30.004 --> 00:02:32.746
As you point your toes,

00:02:32.746 --> 00:02:36.050
you actually end up kind of
putting some force that way

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.700
instead of going this way.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.290
It would kind of take some of your energy

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.749
away from your target.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:48.240
People do do a lot of
pool conditioning now.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.340
You could work on your breath, for sure.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.440
You could work on lung capacity.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.890
I think that would be valuable.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:55.337
You need body conditioning.

00:02:55.337 --> 00:02:57.279
You want to be dense,
you want to be durable.

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.000
If you go into a Muay Thai gym

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.250
and the coach tries to
string you up like that,

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:08.720
get the h--- out of there
as quickly as possible.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.860
Flexibility is important.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.600
You could just lay on your back

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.780
with your legs open facing up on the wall.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:19.370
Or you can have someone

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.200
push down when you do a butterfly stretch.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.550
They push down on your thighs,

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.192
and you try to close them.

00:03:27.488 --> 00:03:28.862
[groans]

00:03:28.862 --> 00:03:32.060
[laughs]

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.450
I've never seen anybody
throw coconuts at someone

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:35.670
to train their core.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:37.670
But I have seen,

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.320
you hit people with medicine balls.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.490
You kind of take the medicine ball,

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.380
and you're like [grunts in rhythm]

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.480
as you do your sit-ups and your crunches.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:48.220
Or they put a glove on
and they'll punch you.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.200
Oftentimes, too, you'll
stand with your hands

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.770
behind your back, and
then they'll just kick.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.740
I'll give it 4. It's important to stretch,

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.710
yes, it's important to
develop lung capacity,

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.100
it's important to have a strong core,

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.120
but the way they're going about it

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.733
is totally not anything
that I've seen done ever.

00:04:10.486 --> 00:04:11.813
His teep is beautiful.

00:04:11.813 --> 00:04:14.213
The teep is a foot jab.

00:04:14.213 --> 00:04:17.146
You can see it starts from his back leg,

00:04:17.146 --> 00:04:19.787
comes up his body, and goes, pat,

00:04:19.787 --> 00:04:21.760
right out through the lead leg.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.390
That would be the position you'd be in

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:24.380
in a Muay Thai fight.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:26.030
But, yeah, a teep is
good if somebody keeps

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.050
coming in on you and
you want to get space.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.550
A high kick to the head looks cool,

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.290
and if you have a nice head
kick, it's a great knockout.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.970
But for me, I prefer to kick to the body.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.210
With the head kick, if you
hit with the top of your foot

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:42.980
to somebody's skull, yes, it hurts them,

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:44.690
but, yes, it hurts you too.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.370
And I'm not trying to be
limping around, you know,

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:50.503
with a messed-up foot for
a month after that fight.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:55.710
For Muay Thai, I've
never seen that stance.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.750
Because he was really,
really low to the ground.

00:04:58.750 --> 00:04:59.720
It's never that low.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.785
I guess that's Boran.

00:05:01.785 --> 00:05:06.000
And so they do more of that,
and I'm just more straight up.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.190
The logic in Muay Thai
of standing taller is

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.170
as you're getting kicked

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.860
and as you want access to your kicks,

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.730
the lower you are, the
longer it's going to take

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.240
to get your leg up there.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.140
But if you're already standing taller,

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:18.398
you can just rotate your
body, and it's there.

00:05:20.134 --> 00:05:23.950
If you can catch their chin,
yes, it's a short night.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.400
I've had a lot of knee surgeries.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:28.010
Probably not in the cards
for me, unfortunately.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.970
But what I find is awesome about knees

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:35.200
is when you're lighting somebody
up with knees to the body,

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.140
it actually takes the fight out of them,

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.880
kind of tenderizes the meat.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:41.800
And his form is perfect in his knees.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:45.780
By rotating the femur in, then
your lower half of your leg

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.520
and your foot goes kind of outward.

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.720
Then you point your toes,

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:51.650
and it creates a much more lancing effect.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.050
And you can also get more
range on your knee too,

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.860
which keeps you further away from danger

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:58.360
as you're implementing damage.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.050
So, those punches were terrible,
but it's a stunt scene.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.827
I did one stunt scene, and I was like,

00:06:04.827 --> 00:06:07.680
"Oh, this is not even real at all."

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.060
For a film, you'd want
to take it out and around

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:12.135
so you can really see it and sell it.

00:06:12.135 --> 00:06:14.400
But when you're actually fighting,

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.290
you want to just keep
it tight to your body.

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.215
Don't want to lift your elbow.

00:06:17.215 --> 00:06:19.956
Just want to rotate, just disguise it.

00:06:19.956 --> 00:06:22.174
Because the more you have a tell,

00:06:22.174 --> 00:06:23.380
the more your opponent sees it

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.847
and they can prepare for that.

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:29.511
That is accurate, the knee shield,

00:06:29.511 --> 00:06:31.636
keeping somebody off you.

00:06:31.636 --> 00:06:34.663
That is definitely a
legitimate thing to get space.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.680
I firmly believe he can jump up there

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.530
and put both his knees like that.

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:46.920
But, yeah, that's not
happening in a fight.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:47.930
That's too much of a gamble.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:49.620
I mean, you're spending
a lot of time in air.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.610
You could stay on the ground
and just drive forward

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.118
and slam an elbow into their face.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.360
And they bow. Yeah, that's accurate too.

00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:05.143
Always bow to an opponent,
whether you win or you lose.

00:07:05.143 --> 00:07:08.636
I have to rate it high,
because it's Tony Jaa.

00:07:08.636 --> 00:07:11.474
So I have to say 9 out of 10.

00:07:11.474 --> 00:07:13.910
You mean you're going to
fight me using Muay Thai?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.100
Not only am I going to use it,

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.057
I'm going to rearrange your face with it!

00:07:17.057 --> 00:07:20.420
A Mongkhon is something that you wear.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.760
Your teacher gives it to you.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.410
You do not fight with it on.
It's for spiritual reasons,

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:27.830
and then you can't go
under the ropes wearing it.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:30.440
It's disrespectful. You've
got to go over the ropes.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:31.715
And when you fight, you take it off.

00:07:34.135 --> 00:07:36.530
That's it! The invincible tiger knee blow

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:37.850
that made him famous!

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:41.580
I've never in my life
come across a tiger knee.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.763
It's a knee, buddy.

00:07:42.763 --> 00:07:44.129
It's just a plain old knee.

00:07:44.129 --> 00:07:47.180
It is absolutely effective to
knee somebody in the stomach.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.963
It is absolutely effective

00:07:48.963 --> 00:07:52.850
to add momentum with a flying knee.

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:54.440
And it's not as risky,

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:57.340
because your feet are
still underneath you.

00:07:57.340 --> 00:07:59.370
It's just forward momentum.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.408
I can see Muay Thai has
many levels to be mastered.

00:08:02.408 --> 00:08:03.241
Hiyah!

00:08:03.241 --> 00:08:06.010
The first person, who looked
like they did more damage,

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.520
got whooped by the second person,

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:08.890
who looked like they did less.

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:10.090
And then he talks about, like,

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.570
there's different levels
to Muay Thai to master.

00:08:12.570 --> 00:08:13.600
I don't know what he's talking about.

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.740
It is not, you know, "Kill Bill,"

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.120
when they did that secret
punch to the heart,

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.890
it's a boom, boom, boom,
boom, and punches him,

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.470
and then, you know, kills Bill.

00:08:21.470 --> 00:08:23.160
No, there's nothing like that in Muay Thai

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.410
that I am aware of after 23 years.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.120
I'll give him a 2 because of the Mongkhon.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.270
No, actually I have to take that away,

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:29.970
because he's fighting with it on.

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.211
So 0 out of 10.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.330
Yes, foot stomp. Heck yeah,
definitely do those knees.

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.220
The kick, not as much.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.010
I don't know why you would be kicking

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:43.530
in that really small space.

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:46.230
There's a lot better things you could use.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:50.310
I would do punches, elbows, and knees,

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.820
because those are the
more close-range weapons.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.940
And then the push kick would be good too,

00:08:54.940 --> 00:08:56.320
because they're in front of you.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.870
You wouldn't really do
round kicks and high kicks,

00:08:58.870 --> 00:09:00.720
because you have to go out and around.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:03.950
Like, yeah, no, you want
it to just go this way.

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:07.870
He actually blocked a kick
with his hand, forearm.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:09.153
Don't do that at home, folks.

00:09:09.153 --> 00:09:11.720
Hand or forearm against shin,

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.280
like, look at this, who wins?

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.305
You can get your arm broken,
get your hand broken.

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:22.800
Well, I like that he keeps
trying to cover and block.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:25.780
That would be definitely
what you want to do.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.710
I mean, the hands are kind
of all over the place.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:29.590
Yeah, you don't wanna be ...

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.640
that's not good.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:32.752
If somebody's striking at you,

00:09:32.752 --> 00:09:34.350
you just need your hands up.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.430
I would give it a 6,
because it's basically

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.050
if you have a hallway in your house

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.767
and you're going to
have a full-blown fight.

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:48.650
So, what they're doing is
they're doing the Wai Khru,

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:52.460
or Ram Muay, and they
have the Mongkhons on,

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.770
and it's a spiritual dance.

00:09:54.770 --> 00:09:56.550
They're definitely doing that correctly.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.340
But, so, it's hard to say.

00:09:58.340 --> 00:10:01.906
Every school has a different dance

00:10:01.906 --> 00:10:03.331
specific to their school.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.800
This clinch part is correct.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:13.760
This is the grappling
portion of a Muay Thai fight.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:18.050
So, you seek to control
position with your hands

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.280
and your arms and your head.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.830
He has him like this.
He's controlling the arm.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:26.600
The other arm's over here,
and his hand is over here

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:28.680
on the side of that guy's neck.

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:32.020
You find control by either
bringing them closer to you

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.840
and deliver strikes at the same time,

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:37.300
or by creating space and making a frame.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.973
With experienced pros, they're
not going to do all this.

00:10:40.973 --> 00:10:42.865
It's going to be more controlled.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.490
Uh-uh. You don't do that.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.178
You're going to eat a
nice hard piece of bone,

00:10:52.178 --> 00:10:53.590
and it's not going to feel good.

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.680
He was standing in front of a Thai fighter

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.610
in a Thai fight with their hands up.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.840
And he was in front of the Thai fighter

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:01.830
punching with his hands down.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.950
You would never do that.
That's elbow range.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:05.416
You would need to have your hands up.

00:11:10.151 --> 00:11:12.210
Oh, and then he swept
him. That was correct.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.610
There's a bunch of different
ways you can sweep them.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:19.460
So he grabbed the leg, lifted
the leg, and turned him.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.210
You can also sweep your opponent

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:25.982
by either body locking and
getting an angle and dumping,

00:11:25.982 --> 00:11:28.270
or as they knee, you sweep their leg.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:30.750
You can take them back over your thigh

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.900
if you get an angle on them.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.409
I give it 8 out of 10.
That was pretty good.

00:11:40.445 --> 00:11:43.300
[Miriam laughs]

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.480
Yeah, this is totally not realistic.

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:47.500
I'm just here for that outfit.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:49.440
The performer is doing elbows,

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.420
and they're elbowing like this.

00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:54.150
The thing with elbows is
if you're in elbow range

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.750
and you're elbowing, they have elbows too.

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.108
So you never want to throw an elbow

00:11:59.108 --> 00:12:00.916
with the other hand down,

00:12:00.916 --> 00:12:02.130
because that's,

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:03.753
you would be cut open.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:07.020
That kick was really silly.

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:09.625
He's just spinning around
lifting the leg up.

00:12:09.625 --> 00:12:12.530
But it's like, even with a
punch, it's not just about this.

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:14.178
Kicking is not just lifting the leg.

00:12:14.178 --> 00:12:16.570
It starts at your foot
connection to the ground

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:18.830
and the rotation of your foot.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.066
And it's like, your foot, your ankle,

00:12:21.066 --> 00:12:22.710
your knee, then your hip.

00:12:22.710 --> 00:12:25.200
And then the last bit is this.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:27.110
And so the same thing
with a Muay Thai kick.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:28.210
If you want to kick with the right side,

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.180
it starts with the left
side of your body, actually.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.412
You want to rotate the
opposite side of your body

00:12:34.412 --> 00:12:38.010
to sling the kick, and
then the leg comes after.

00:12:38.010 --> 00:12:41.070
I know that it's stunts and
you have to kind of cheat it,

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:44.360
but you still can make
it so it looks right

00:12:44.360 --> 00:12:46.410
instead of kind of flailing.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.043
2 out of 10.

00:12:48.043 --> 00:12:50.226
That was, like, all completely off.

